  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 302.9 K, melting point of Ga; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.336$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $Cp^o = 8.561 + 0.298x10^{-3}T - 0.854x10^5T^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o - H_{298}^o = 8.561x10^{-3}T + 0.149x10^{-6}T^2 + 0.854x10^2T^{-1} - 2.852$ </td></tr></table>\nFormation equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-302.9 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = 40.270 - 1.550 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.202 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 62.800 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 40.270 + 1.550 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 0.202 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 31.400 \\text{T}^{-1} - 31.046 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">302.9-2000 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = 38.564 - 1.054 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.228 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 130.000 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 38.564 + 1.054 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T + 0.228 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 65.000 \\text{T}^{-1} - 22.955 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Pedley (396). ",
    "lines_raw": [
